Floor Sum / Divisor Block Decomposition

Core Concept
The value of N / x (floor division) takes at most 2 * sqrt(N) distinct values for x from 1 to N.
We group values of x that give the same quotient 'val' into contiguous blocks [l, r], where r = N / val.

Time Complexity: O(sqrt(N))

Space Complexity: O(1)

Code Templates

Template A: Counting Divisors Sum (e.g., A * B + C = N)

ll count_divisors_sum(ll n) {
        int cur=1 , res=0;
        while (cur<=n) {
            int val = n/cur ;
            res+= val *(n/val+1-cur);
            cur=n/val+1;
        }
return res;
}

Template B: Sum of Divisor Values (e.g., Sum of sigma(i))

long long sum_of_divisors(long long n) {
long long cur = 1, res = 0;
while (cur <= n) {
long long val = n / cur;
long long r = n / val;

    long long sum_lr = (cur + r) * (r - cur + 1) / 2; // AP sum
    res += val * sum_lr;
    cur = r + 1;
}
return res;
}

Applications

Equation Problems: Reducible to A * B <= N or A * B + C = N.

Divisor Functions: Computing sum of all divisors of all numbers from 1 to n.

3-Variable Equations (A * B * C <= N): Loop A up to N^(1/3), then use O(sqrt(N/A)) block decomposition.

Mobius Inversion / Coprime Counting: Optimizing sum(mu(i) * f(N/i)).
